+# Specialty Directory Composed in Memory from Two Reads
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+The specialty directory lists every specialty the clinic knows, each with the veterinarians holding it. A specialty that no veterinarian holds is still listed.
+
+The `@ManyToMany` association runs one way, from `Vet` to `Specialty`. A specialty therefore cannot reach its holders. No repository exists for `Specialty`, so the unheld ones are unreachable from the veterinarian rows alone.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Inverse mapping** — add a `mappedBy` collection of veterinarians to `Specialty` and navigate from the specialty.
+2. **Projection query** — one JPQL query joining specialties to veterinarians, shaped in the repository.
+3. **Two reads composed in memory** — read the specialties and the veterinarians separately, group them in a value object.
+
+## Decision
+
+Option 3. A new `SpecialtyRepository` returns every specialty in name order. The existing `VetRepository.findAll()` supplies the holders. A `SpecialtyDirectory` value object groups them by a pure static factory.
+
+Option 1 changes the `Vet` fetch graph and the cached veterinarian list, which this slice's non-goals exclude. Option 2 moves the shaping into a query string that no test can exercise without a database. Option 3 keeps the grouping a pure function over real objects.
+
+`SpecialtyDirectory` carries a specialty name and the full names of its holders, not entity references. Names give the value object equality by value, which entity references would not.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Both edge cases are structural rather than conditional. Iterating specialties lists an unheld one; grouping by specialty names no veterinarian who holds none.
+- The grouping and the full-name form are unit-testable without MVC or a database.
+- The web controller keeps no business rule, and the veterinarian directory, its eager fetch, and the `vets` cache are untouched.
+- Every specialty and every veterinarian is read per request. The product decision excludes paging, which is acceptable at clinic scale.
+- The specialty read is uncached while the veterinarian read is cached under `vets`. A specialty added out of band appears before a change to its holders does.
+- The directory carries names only. A later link to a veterinarian's page needs identity added to the entry.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md § Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts) — the types this decision introduces
+- [2026-07-31-feature-package-organization.md](2026-07-31-feature-package-organization.md) — why the new types sit in the `vet` feature package
+- [2026-07-31-relational-persistence-with-spring-data-jpa.md](2026-07-31-relational-persistence-with-spring-data-jpa.md) — the repository style the new repository follows
