 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-specialtydirectory-001"></a>
+
+The clinic also publishes the directory the other way round. One page lists every specialty the clinic knows, each under its stored name, with the veterinarians holding it `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` (stated by the owner 2026-08-16). Every specialty appears on that one page, without paging. A veterinarian is named in full, first name then last name. A veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on the page; the page lists specialties, not the whole roster. The page is reachable at its own address alone: nothing in the navigation names it, and no other page links to it. Its wording is presented in the reader's language like every other page `[REQ-LANG-002]`.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened, then every one is listed under its stored name on a single page.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given a specialty that veterinarians hold, when the directory is opened, then each holder is named first name then last name.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is named nowhere on the page.
+- `[REQ-SPECIALTYDIRECTORY-001]` given any other page of the system, when it is rendered, then it carries no navigation entry and no link to the specialty directory.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty that no veterinarian holds is still listed, with no veterinarian named under it.
+2. When the clinic knows no specialty at all, the page renders with no specialties rather than failing.
+3. Specialties are listed in a stable order, as are the veterinarians within each specialty.
+
